# Working rules

Read `{{RULES_DIR}}workflow.md` before anything else. Every rule below has one home; the
router links, it does not restate.

## Non-negotiables

- **Run the relevant suite before reporting done.** If it fails, paste the failure — do not
  describe it, do not report done. "Done" is defined in `{{RULES_DIR}}workflow.md`.
- **Stay in scope.** Fix what was asked. Note adjacent problems; don't silently fix them.
- **Conventional commits**, one logical change each, only when asked — the `commit` skill.
- **A convention change edits its `{{RULES_DIR}}` file in the same commit.** A rule that lives
  only in a diff is a rule the next agent will break.
- **One fact, one home.** If something belongs in a pattern file, link it — don't restate it.
- **Comments only where the code cannot say it.** Default to none. No docstring that repeats
  the signature, no comment that narrates a diff, none that refers to something removed.
- **No Claude/Codex/Cursor as co-author** on commits.
- **Confirm before writing migration or backward-compatibility code.** It is often an unused
  feature.
- **Ask when readings diverge; decide when one is obviously right, and say which** —
  `{{RULES_DIR}}workflow.md` has the ask/decide table.

